The auditors flagged only the scope label. The claim describes how SDSA proceeds and what it produces, so S2 fits. The evidence says the intermediate is "suspended into an NCO", which is garbled wording. I read it as resolved into a noncrossover product, as the original atom did. I keep that reading but do not add a mechanism for it. I cite both sentences.


{"atoms":[{"statement":"In synthesis-dependent strand annealing (SDSA), no more than one end invades, which leads to a single Holliday junction, and this intermediate structure proceeds to a noncrossover (NCO) product.","scope":"S2","evidence_ids":["MED-PATH-p0122-s25","MED-PATH-p0122-s26"]}],"note":"Scope changed from S3 to S2 because the atom describes how SDSA works and what it yields, not a limit or boundary. The evidence phrase 'suspended into an NCO' is read as the intermediate leading to a noncrossover product."}
